#!/usr/bin/env bb
;; IDENTITY: every driver arm, every document, one answer.   kin/scripts/identity   (DEVLOG P2.2, SPEC 14.1.5)
;;
;; The corpus is a list of (input, transcript) pairs. Every host's driver (`emon-rs` on Rust, `emon-go` on Go)
;; converts each input and prints the BUNDLE (`--out=bundle`: the compact and the pretty JSON, the default and
;; the full HTML, the text layer's evidence dump and the stage-0 intake line, one conversion). What must hold,
;; per input, in bytes:
;;
;;   1. every ARM gives the reference's bundle: the same host's other byte-source adapters (Rust: bytes, Read +
;;      Seek, spooled Read; Go: bytes, `*os.File` as `io.ReaderAt`, io.ReadSeeker, spooled io.Reader), the other
;;      host's, and each host over a 512-byte-chunk ASYNC source (the cache misses, the loop fetches and re-runs:
;;      D058). Exit code and stderr are part of the answer, so an input that fails (damaged, encrypted, an image,
;;      a wrong password) must fail the same way, by the same name, on every arm;
;;   2. the TRANSCRIPT, empty in this phase (the slice issues no requests, D089) but not absent: each host's
;;      `--record` writes the same directory, byte for byte, and each host REPLAYS the other's to the reference
;;      bundle (SPEC 14.1.5: the pair is (input bytes, transcript), replayed anywhere).
;;
;; The corpus: every committed PDF under `test/` (the synthetic documents and their scans, the fixtures of the PDF
;; layer, the repaired and encrypted ones, the tagged ones, the fuzz crashers), each (file, password) row of
;; `test/pdf/p3.txt` (wrong passwords included), the image fixtures of `test/image/` (P6.1, D187-D190: PNG, JPEG, TIFF,
;; multi-page TIFF, and the refusals, each converted to pages by both hosts), and two small PNGs.
;; For a JPEG the two hosts' live decoders may differ in the last bits (D190), so their transcripts differ in those
;; pixels: their `transcript.edn` must still be the same, and each host must replay the OTHER's transcript to the
;; same bundle (the decode answer through the transcript is what makes a JPEG's replay identical, D089).
;;
;;   bb identity                        the gate: every document, the five-and-four arms above, in parallel
;;   bb identity --full                 also: more chunk sizes (7, 100, 4096) async and sync, on both hosts
;;   bb identity --corpus [--limit N] [--sample K]   INSTEAD the PDFs of `corpus/` (never committed): a non-gate, slow
;;   bb identity --only SUBSTR          documents whose path contains SUBSTR
;;
;; AND WITH `assets` ON (P3.13, SPEC 14.1.5, D117): the same arms and the same transcript trip over the documents that have
;; images (P3.12's fixtures and the synthetic documents with pictures), each given `--assets=images`: the bundle then also has
;; the HTML in `external` and `omit` mode and every asset file, byte for byte (hex), so the asset files and the three HTML
;; modes are identical on every arm, in memory and through the 512-byte async source (a gate of its own below).
;;
;; THE BROWSER (P9.3, D356) is a host too, when the WASM toolchain is there: the Rust host built for wasm32 and driven by the JS SDK in
;; a headless Chrome (`test/driver/wasm/`). Every input goes through five byte-source adapters (an ArrayBuffer, a Blob, a URL read by
;; `Range` from a local server, a spooled ReadableStream, and a `{size, read}` over 512-byte chunks whose every read is a promise: the
;; engine misses, the JS loop awaits and runs it again), each to the reference bundle, exit code and stderr (`--full`: also a
;; Uint8Array view, a File, a custom source and an ArrayBuffer read by range); then the browser RECORDS a transcript (the same
;; directory as Rust's, byte for byte) and REPLAYS Rust's to the reference bundle. With `assets` on (`images`, and since
;; P9.5 `figures` too), the asset documents run through it as well (from their committed transcripts where a codec image needs one): the HTML in
;; three modes and every asset file. Without the toolchain (`kin/scripts/emon-wasm-run` exits 3: no nightly with rust-src, Node 22, Chrome, or the JS
;; devDependencies) the arm is left out, loudly; EMON_SKIP_WASM=1 leaves it out on purpose.
;;
;; THE JAVA HOST (P9.1, D449) is a third host when a JDK 22+ is there: four arms (bytes, a SeekableByteChannel, a spooled
;; InputStream, a 512-byte async source), its transcript equal to Rust's (directory, byte for byte; a JPEG's PNGs apart, as for
;; Go), its replay of Rust's transcript, and Rust's replay of its transcript, each to the reference bundle. Without a JDK
;; (`kin/scripts/emon-java-build` exits 3) the arm is left out, loudly; EMON_SKIP_JAVA=1 leaves it out on purpose.
;;
;; THE C# HOST (P9.2, D457) is a fourth host when a .NET 8+ SDK is there: the same four arms (bytes, a seekable FileStream, a spooled
;; forward-only Stream, a 512-byte async source), its transcript equal to Rust's (directory, byte for byte; a JPEG's PNGs apart), its
;; replay of Rust's transcript, and Rust's replay of its transcript, each to the reference bundle. Without an SDK
;; (`kin/scripts/emon-cs-build` exits 3) the arm is left out, loudly; EMON_SKIP_CSHARP=1 leaves it out on purpose.
;;
;; THE C BINDING (P9.4, D473) is a fifth driver when a C compiler is there: `emon-c`, a C program over libemon (the Rust host behind
;; host/c/include/emon.h). Five arms: the one-shot call over bytes, over a LAZY pread source, over a spooled stream, the inverted step API
;; (emon_open/step/provide/finish), and the step API over 512-byte chunks that miss and re-run; its transcript (the step API with record=1)
;; equal to Rust's (directory, byte for byte), its replay of Rust's, and Rust's replay of its transcript. Without a C compiler
;; (`kin/scripts/emon-c-build` exits 3) the arm is left out, loudly; EMON_SKIP_C=1 leaves it out on purpose.
;;
;; THE BABASHKA POD (P9.4, D475) is a sixth: the pod (a Rust binary over the Rust host) loaded by babashka, driven by `test/driver/pod/emon-pod`
;; through `emon/convert`. Two arms: the file as a path (the pod reads it lazily) and as base64 bytes. A pod converts in one call, so it has
;; no async source and no transcript: the arms that need those, and the inputs that replay a committed transcript, leave it out.
;; EMON_SKIP_POD=1 leaves it out on purpose.
;;
;; THE COVERAGE CHECK (P9.5, D494): after each pass the gate adds up WHAT EACH HOST RAN (a ledger per input: every [host arm] it was run on, every one it was
;; not, with the reason) and FAILS when a host that is present ran an arm on fewer inputs than the pass has without a skip that says why. The skips are
;; printed as `note` lines: the pod's, which converts in one call and so has no transcript to record or replay (it is not run on an input that is run from a
;; committed transcript, nor does it join the record/replay trip); the transcript trip itself is not made for an input that is refused or run from a
;; committed transcript, on any host. The browser has its own pass over the same inputs at all three levels (the plain corpus, `images`, `figures`).
;;
;; A difference prints the first differing section and byte offset, and the arms.
(require '[babashka.fs :as fs]
         '[babashka.process :refer [process shell destroy-tree]]
         '[cheshire.core :as json]
         '[clojure.string :as str])

(def fails (atom 0))
(defn ok [& xs] (println (str "  ok   " (apply str xs))))
(defn bad [& xs] (swap! fails inc) (println (str "  FAIL " (apply str xs))))

(def args (vec *command-line-args*))
(def full? (some #{"--full"} args))
(def corpus? (some #{"--corpus"} args))
(defn opt [k] (some->> (map-indexed vector args) (some (fn [[i a]] (when (= a k) (get args (inc i)))))))
(def only (opt "--only"))
(def extra (atom []))   ; flags every arm is given (the assets pass sets one)
(def limit (some-> (opt "--limit") parse-long))
(def sample (some-> (opt "--sample") parse-long))

(shell {:out :string :err :string} "kin/scripts/emit")
(defn build [script what]
  (let [r @(process {:out :string :err :string} script)]
    (if (zero? (:exit r))
      (str/trim (:out r))
      (do (println "  FAIL the" what "driver did not build:\n" (:err r)) (System/exit 1)))))
(def rust (build "kin/scripts/emon-rs-build" "Rust"))
(def go (build "kin/scripts/emon-go-build" "Go"))
;; THE JAVA ARM (P9.1, D449) is optional: `emon-java-build` exits 3 with `SKIP java -- why` on stderr when there is no JDK 22+
;; (`EMON_JDK`, /opt/homebrew/opt/openjdk, `java_home`), and the arm is then left out, LOUDLY, and nothing fails. `EMON_SKIP_JAVA=1` leaves it out on purpose.
(def java
  (if (System/getenv "EMON_SKIP_JAVA")
    (do (println "  SKIP java arm -- EMON_SKIP_JAVA is set") nil)
    (let [r @(process {:out :string :err :string} "kin/scripts/emon-java-build")]
      (case (:exit r)
        0 (str/trim (:out r))
        3 (do (println (str "  " (str/trim (:err r)) " (the Java arm is left out)")) nil)
        (do (println "  FAIL the Java driver did not build:\n" (:err r)) (System/exit 1))))))
;; THE C# ARM (P9.2, D457) is optional: `emon-cs-build` exits 3 with `SKIP csharp -- why` on stderr when there is no .NET 8+ SDK (`EMON_DOTNET`, dotnet on
;; the PATH, /opt/homebrew/bin, ~/.dotnet), and the arm is then left out, LOUDLY, and nothing fails. `EMON_SKIP_CSHARP=1` leaves it out on purpose.
(def csharp
  (if (System/getenv "EMON_SKIP_CSHARP")
    (do (println "  SKIP csharp arm -- EMON_SKIP_CSHARP is set") nil)
    (let [r @(process {:out :string :err :string} "kin/scripts/emon-cs-build")]
      (case (:exit r)
        0 (str/trim (:out r))
        3 (do (println (str "  " (str/trim (:err r)) " (the C# arm is left out)")) nil)
        (do (println "  FAIL the C# driver did not build:\n" (:err r)) (System/exit 1))))))
;; THE C ARM (P9.4, D473) is optional: `emon-c-build` exits 3 with `SKIP c -- why` on stderr when there is no C compiler, and the arm is then left out,
;; LOUDLY, and nothing fails. `EMON_SKIP_C=1` leaves it out on purpose.
(def cbind
  (let [r @(process {:out :string :err :string} "kin/scripts/emon-c-build")]
    (case (:exit r)
      0 (str/trim (:out r))
      3 (do (println (str "  " (str/trim (:err r)) " (the C arm is left out)")) nil)
      (do (println "  FAIL the C driver did not build:\n" (:err r)) (System/exit 1)))))
;; THE POD ARM (P9.4, D475) is optional the same way (`emon-pod-build` exits 3 with `SKIP pod -- why`).
(def pod
  (let [r @(process {:out :string :err :string} "kin/scripts/emon-pod-build")]
    (case (:exit r)
      0 (str/trim (:out r))
      3 (do (println (str "  " (str/trim (:err r)) " (the pod arm is left out)")) nil)
      (do (println "  FAIL the pod did not build:\n" (:err r)) (System/exit 1)))))
;; THE BROWSER ARM (P9.3, D356) is optional: `emon-wasm-run --check` exits 3 with `SKIP wasm -- why` on stderr when the toolchain is
;; missing, and the arm is then left out, LOUDLY, and nothing fails.
(def wasm
  (let [r @(process {:out :string :err :string} "kin/scripts/emon-wasm-run" "--check")]
    (case (:exit r)
      0 (str/trim (:out r))
      3 (do (println (str "  " (str/trim (:err r)) " (the wasm arm is left out)")) nil)
      (do (println "  FAIL the wasm module did not build:\n" (:err r)) (System/exit 1)))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- the corpus

(defn p3-rows []
  (->> (str/split-lines (slurp "test/pdf/p3.txt"))
       (remove #(or (str/blank? %) (str/starts-with? % "#")))
       (map #(str/split % #"\t"))
       (map (fn [[f pw]] {:file (str "test/" f) :pw (when (not= pw "-") pw)}))
       distinct))

(defn globs [dir pat] (sort (map str (fs/glob dir pat))))

(def corpus
  (if corpus?
    ;; the never-committed public corpus (a symlink in a worktree: follow it)
    (let [all (sort (map str (fs/glob "corpus" "**/*.pdf" {:follow-links true})))
          all (if sample (take-nth (max 1 (quot (count all) sample)) all) all)]
      (mapv (fn [f] {:file f :pw nil}) (cond->> all limit (take limit))))
    (let [p3 (p3-rows)
          p3files (set (map :file p3))
          plain (fn [fs] (map (fn [f] {:file f :pw nil}) fs))]
      (vec (concat (plain (remove p3files (globs "test" "**/*.pdf")))
                   p3
                   (plain (globs "test/image" "*.{png,jpg,tif}"))
                   (plain ["test/ocr/h-keyword/bitmap-0000.png" "test/corpus/synth/html/img/initial-W.png"]))))))

(def corpus* (if only (filterv #(str/includes? (:file %) only) corpus) corpus))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------------ the arms

(def chunk-arms
  (if full?
    [["async7" ["--chunk=7" "--async"]] ["async100" ["--chunk=100" "--async"]] ["async4096" ["--chunk=4096" "--async"]]
     ["sync64" ["--chunk=64" "--source=seek"]]]
    []))

;; [host name args]; the first is the reference
(def arms
  (vec (concat
        [[:rust "bytes" []]
         [:rust "seek" ["--source=seek"]]
         [:rust "spool" ["--source=spool"]]
         [:rust "async512" ["--chunk=512" "--async"]]
         [:go "bytes" []]
         [:go "readerat" ["--source=readerat"]]
         [:go "seek" ["--source=seek"]]
         [:go "spool" ["--source=spool"]]
         [:go "async512" ["--chunk=512" "--async"]]]
        ;; the Java host's four arms: a byte[], a SeekableByteChannel (also what `readerat` is in Java), a spooled InputStream, a 512-byte async source
        (when java
          [[:java "bytes" []]
           [:java "seek" ["--source=seek"]]
           [:java "spool" ["--source=spool"]]
           [:java "async512" ["--chunk=512" "--async"]]])
        ;; the C# host's four arms: a byte[], a seekable FileStream (also what `readerat` is in C#), a spooled forward-only Stream, a 512-byte async source
        (when csharp
          [[:csharp "bytes" []]
           [:csharp "seek" ["--source=seek"]]
           [:csharp "spool" ["--source=spool"]]
           [:csharp "async512" ["--chunk=512" "--async"]]])
        ;; the C driver's five arms (P9.4): the one-shot over bytes, over a lazy pread source, over a spooled stream, the step API, the step API over 512-byte chunks
        (when cbind
          [[:c "bytes" []]
           [:c "seek" ["--source=seek"]]
           [:c "spool" ["--source=spool"]]
           [:c "step" ["--source=step"]]
           [:c "async512" ["--chunk=512" "--async"]]])
        ;; the pod's two (P9.4): a path (read lazily) and base64 bytes
        (when pod
          [[:pod "bytes" []]
           [:pod "path" ["--source=seek"]]])
        (for [h (cond-> [:rust :go] java (conj :java) csharp (conj :csharp) cbind (conj :c)) [n a] chunk-arms] [h n a]))))

(defn drive
  "Run a driver: {:exit :out (bytes) :err}. A run that takes over two minutes is killed (our own process)."
  [host args {:keys [file pw replay]}]
  (let [exe (case host :rust rust :go go :java java :csharp csharp :c cbind :pod pod)
        p (apply process {:out :bytes :err :string}
                 exe "--out=bundle" (concat args @extra (when pw [(str "--password=" pw)]) (when replay [(str "--replay=" replay)]) [file]))
        r (deref p 120000 ::timeout)]
    (if (= r ::timeout)
      (do (destroy-tree p) {:exit -1 :out (byte-array 0) :err "TIMEOUT"})
      {:exit (:exit r) :out (let [o (:out r)] (if (bytes? o) o (.getBytes (str o)))) :err (:err r)})))

(defn same? [a b]
  (and (= (:exit a) (:exit b)) (= (:err a) (:err b)) (java.util.Arrays/equals ^bytes (:out a) ^bytes (:out b))))

(defn first-diff
  "Where two answers first differ: the section of the bundle and the byte offset in it."
  [a b]
  (cond
    (not= (:exit a) (:exit b)) (str "exit " (:exit a) " vs " (:exit b))
    (not= (:err a) (:err b)) (str "stderr " (pr-str (subs (:err a) 0 (min 120 (count (:err a))))) " vs " (pr-str (subs (:err b) 0 (min 120 (count (:err b))))))
    :else (let [x ^bytes (:out a) y ^bytes (:out b)
                n (min (alength x) (alength y))
                i (or (first (filter #(not= (aget x %) (aget y %)) (range n))) n)
                head (String. x 0 (int i) "UTF-8")
                section (or (last (re-seq #"(?m)^== (\S+)$" head)) [nil "(start)"])]
            (str "section " (second section) ", byte " i " of " (alength x) " vs " (alength y)))))

(defn dir-files [d]
  (when (fs/exists? d)
    (into (sorted-map) (for [f (fs/list-dir d)] [(fs/file-name f) (vec (fs/read-all-bytes f))]))))

(def work (str (fs/create-temp-dir {:dir (fs/create-dirs ".cache/identity") :prefix "run."})))
(.addShutdownHook (Runtime/getRuntime) (Thread. (fn [] (fs/delete-tree work))))

(defn one
  "Every arm and the transcript trip for one input: {:probs [problem strings, empty when identical] :outcome :document | the error's name}."
  [i item]
  (let [ref (drive :rust [] item)
        probs (atom [])
        ;; THE LEDGER (P9.5, D494): every [host arm] this input ran on, and every one it was NOT run on, with the reason; `coverage` adds them up
        ran (atom [[:rust "bytes"]])
        skips (atom [])
        note (fn [& xs] (swap! probs conj (apply str xs)))]
    (when (= -1 (:exit ref)) (note "the reference timed out"))
    (doseq [[host name a] (rest arms)]
      (if (and (= host :pod) (:replay item))
        ;; a pod converts in one call: it has no transcript to replay (P9.4)
        (swap! skips conj [host name "the input is run from a committed transcript, and the pod has none to replay"])
        (let [r (drive host a item)]
          (swap! ran conj [host name])
          (when-not (same? ref r)
            (note (clojure.core/name host) "/" name " differs from rust/bytes: " (first-diff ref r))))))
    (when (and (zero? (:exit ref)) (:replay item))
      (doseq [h (cond-> [:rust :go] java (conj :java) csharp (conj :csharp) cbind (conj :c) pod (conj :pod))]
        (swap! skips conj [h "trip" "the input is run from a committed transcript on every arm (its pixels are the recording's), so there is nothing to record"])))
    (when-not (zero? (:exit ref))
      (doseq [h (cond-> [:rust :go] java (conj :java) csharp (conj :csharp) cbind (conj :c) pod (conj :pod))]
        (swap! skips conj [h "trip" (str "the input is refused (" (second (re-find #"error: (\S+)" (:err ref))) "), so there is no transcript to record")])))
    (when pod
      (when (and (zero? (:exit ref)) (not (:replay item)))
        (swap! skips conj [:pod "trip" "a pod converts in one call: it records no transcript and replays none (P9.4)"])))
    ;; the transcript: record on each, compare the directories, replay each on the other (a document whose images the host decodes IS
    ;; given its committed transcript above, on every arm: its pixels are the recording's, so the arms are about everything else)
    (when (and (zero? (:exit ref)) (not (:replay item)))
      (let [rd (str work "/" i "-rust") gd (str work "/" i "-go")
            rr (drive :rust [(str "--record=" rd)] item)
            gr (drive :go [(str "--record=" gd)] item)]
        (when-not (same? ref rr) (note "rust --record changes the answer: " (first-diff ref rr)))
        (when-not (same? ref gr) (note "go --record changes the answer: " (first-diff ref gr)))
        (let [rf (dir-files rd) gf (dir-files gd)
              lossy? (re-find #"(?i)\.jpe?g$" (:file item))
              strip-png (fn [m] (into {} (remove (fn [[k _]] (str/ends-with? k ".png")) m)))]
          (when-not (if lossy? (= (strip-png rf) (strip-png gf) ) (= rf gf))
            (note "the transcripts differ: rust " (some-> rf keys vec) " go " (some-> gf keys vec))))
        (let [gp (drive :go [(str "--replay=" rd)] item)
              rp (drive :rust [(str "--replay=" gd)] item)]
          (swap! ran conj [:rust "trip"] [:go "trip"])
          (when-not (same? ref gp) (note "go replaying rust's transcript differs: " (first-diff ref gp)))
          (when-not (same? ref rp) (note "rust replaying go's transcript differs: " (first-diff ref rp))))
        ;; the Java host (P9.1): it records the same directory, replays Rust's, and Rust replays its
        (when java
          (let [jd (str work "/" i "-java")
                jr (drive :java [(str "--record=" jd)] item)]
            (when-not (same? ref jr) (note "java --record changes the answer: " (first-diff ref jr)))
            (let [rf (dir-files rd) jf (dir-files jd)
                  lossy? (re-find #"(?i)\.jpe?g$" (:file item))
                  strip-png (fn [m] (into {} (remove (fn [[k _]] (str/ends-with? k ".png")) m)))]
              (when-not (if lossy? (= (strip-png rf) (strip-png jf)) (= rf jf))
                (note "the transcripts differ: rust " (some-> rf keys vec) " java " (some-> jf keys vec))))
            (let [jp (drive :java [(str "--replay=" rd)] item)
                  rj (drive :rust [(str "--replay=" jd)] item)
                  _ (swap! ran conj [:java "trip"])]
              (when-not (same? ref jp) (note "java replaying rust's transcript differs: " (first-diff ref jp)))
              (when-not (same? ref rj) (note "rust replaying java's transcript differs: " (first-diff ref rj))))
            (fs/delete-tree jd)))
        ;; the C# host (P9.2): it records the same directory, replays Rust's, and Rust replays its
        (when csharp
          (let [cd (str work "/" i "-csharp")
                cr (drive :csharp [(str "--record=" cd)] item)]
            (when-not (same? ref cr) (note "csharp --record changes the answer: " (first-diff ref cr)))
            (let [rf (dir-files rd) cf (dir-files cd)
                  lossy? (re-find #"(?i)\.jpe?g$" (:file item))
                  strip-png (fn [m] (into {} (remove (fn [[k _]] (str/ends-with? k ".png")) m)))]
              (when-not (if lossy? (= (strip-png rf) (strip-png cf)) (= rf cf))
                (note "the transcripts differ: rust " (some-> rf keys vec) " csharp " (some-> cf keys vec))))
            (let [cp (drive :csharp [(str "--replay=" rd)] item)
                  rc (drive :rust [(str "--replay=" cd)] item)
                  _ (swap! ran conj [:csharp "trip"])]
              (when-not (same? ref cp) (note "csharp replaying rust's transcript differs: " (first-diff ref cp)))
              (when-not (same? ref rc) (note "rust replaying csharp's transcript differs: " (first-diff ref rc))))
            (fs/delete-tree cd)))
        ;; the C binding (P9.4): the step API with record=1 writes the same directory, replays Rust's, and Rust replays its
        (when cbind
          (let [cd (str work "/" i "-c")
                cr (drive :c [(str "--record=" cd)] item)]
            (when-not (same? ref cr) (note "c --record changes the answer: " (first-diff ref cr)))
            (let [rf (dir-files rd) cf (dir-files cd)
                  lossy? (re-find #"(?i)\.jpe?g$" (:file item))
                  strip-png (fn [m] (into {} (remove (fn [[k _]] (str/ends-with? k ".png")) m)))]
              (when-not (if lossy? (= (strip-png rf) (strip-png cf)) (= rf cf))
                (note "the transcripts differ: rust " (some-> rf keys vec) " c " (some-> cf keys vec))))
            (let [cp (drive :c [(str "--replay=" rd)] item)
                  rc (drive :rust [(str "--replay=" cd)] item)
                  _ (swap! ran conj [:c "trip"])]
              (when-not (same? ref cp) (note "c replaying rust's transcript differs: " (first-diff ref cp)))
              (when-not (same? ref rc) (note "rust replaying c's transcript differs: " (first-diff ref rc))))
            (fs/delete-tree cd)))
        (fs/delete-tree rd) (fs/delete-tree gd)))
    {:probs @probs
     :ran @ran
     :skips @skips
     :outcome (if (zero? (:exit ref)) :document (or (second (re-find #"error: (\S+)" (:err ref))) :other))}))

(defn coverage
  "THE COVERAGE CHECK (P9.5, D494): did every host see every input on every arm? Adds up the ledgers of a pass's results: a [host arm] that ran on fewer
  inputs than the pass has, without a skip that says why, FAILS; the skips (reason and count) are printed. Answers the printed summary."
  [label results]
  (let [n (count results)
        ran (frequencies (mapcat (comp :ran second) results))
        skipped (frequencies (map (fn [[h a why]] [h a why]) (mapcat (comp :skips second) results)))
        skipped-by (reduce (fn [m [[h a _] c]] (update m [h a] (fnil + 0) c)) {} skipped)
        ;; the transcript trip is for the inputs that convert from no committed transcript; every other [host arm] is for EVERY input
        trips-expected (- n (reduce + 0 (for [[_ r] results :when (some (fn [[h a _]] (and (= h :rust) (= a "trip"))) (:skips r))] 1)))
        short (for [[h a] (distinct (map #(subvec % 0 2) (concat (keys ran) (keys skipped-by))))
                    :let [want (- n (get skipped-by [h a] 0))
                          got (get ran [h a] 0)]
                    :when (not= want got)]
                [h a got want])]
    (doseq [[h a got want] short] (bad "[" label "] coverage: " (name h) "/" a " ran on " got " inputs, " want " expected"))
    (doseq [[[h a why] c] (sort-by (comp str key) skipped) :when (or (not= a "trip") (= h :pod))]   ; (a trip skipped for a refused input or a committed transcript is the same for every host)
      (println (str "  note [" label "] " (name h) "/" a " skipped on " c " of " n " inputs: " why)))
    (let [hosts (distinct (map first (keys ran)))
          per (for [h hosts]
                (let [arms* (filter (fn [[hh _]] (= hh h)) (keys ran))]
                  (str (name h) " " (count (remove #(= "trip" (second %)) arms*)) " arms"
                       (when (some #(= "trip" (second %)) arms*) (str " + trip on " (get ran [h "trip"]) "/" trips-expected)))))]
      (str (str/join ", " per) " over " n " inputs"))))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------ the browser arm (P9.3, D356)

(def wasm-adapters
  (if full?
    ["array" "u8" "blob" "file" "url" "stream" "custom" "lazy" "async512"]
    ["array" "blob" "url" "stream" "async512"]))

(defn- wasm-batch
  "One batch of [i item ref rd] through the browser: every adapter, the browser's own recording and its replay of Rust's. Answers the problems, as
  [file text] pairs, and how many jobs ran."
  [label base batch]
  (let [assets? (seq @extra)
        base-job (fn [i item id adapter]
                   (cond-> {:id id :path (:file item) :adapter adapter}
                     (:pw item) (assoc :password (:pw item))
                     assets? (assoc :assets (if (some #{"--assets=figures"} @extra) "figures" "images"))))
        jobs (vec (concat
                   (for [[i item _ _] batch a wasm-adapters]
                     (cond-> (base-job i item (str i "-" a) a)
                       (:replay item) (assoc :replayDir (:replay item) :replay (mapv fs/file-name (fs/list-dir (:replay item))))))
                   (for [[i item _ rd] batch :when rd kind [:rec :rep]]
                     (cond-> (base-job i item (str i "-" (name kind)) "array")
                       (= kind :rec) (assoc :record true)
                       (= kind :rep) (assoc :replayDir rd :replay (mapv fs/file-name (fs/list-dir rd)))))))
        jf (str base "/jobs.json")
        outd (str base "/out")]
    (fs/delete-tree outd)
    (spit jf (json/generate-string jobs))
    (let [r @(process {:out :string :err :string :extra-env {"EMON_WASM_MODULE" wasm}} "kin/scripts/emon-wasm-run" "--jobs" jf "--out" outd)]
      (when-not (zero? (:exit r))
        (println "  FAIL the browser driver failed:\n" (:err r))
        (System/exit 1)))
    (let [answer (fn [id] {:exit (parse-long (slurp (str outd "/" id ".exit")))
                           :err (slurp (str outd "/" id ".err"))
                           :out (.getBytes ^String (slurp (str outd "/" id ".out")) "UTF-8")})
          probs (atom [])]
      (doseq [[i item ref rd] batch]
        (let [note (fn [& xs] (swap! probs conj [(:file item) (apply str xs)]))]
          (doseq [a wasm-adapters]
            (let [r (answer (str i "-" a))]
              (when-not (same? ref r) (note "wasm/" a " differs from rust/bytes: " (first-diff ref r)))))
          (when rd
            (let [rec (answer (str i "-rec"))
                  rep (answer (str i "-rep"))
                  rf (dir-files rd)
                  wf (dir-files (str outd "/" i "-rec.transcript"))
                  lossy? (re-find #"(?i)\.jpe?g$" (:file item))
                  strip-png (fn [m] (into {} (remove (fn [[k _]] (str/ends-with? k ".png")) m)))]
              (when-not (same? ref rec) (note "wasm record changes the answer: " (first-diff ref rec)))
              (when-not (if lossy? (= (strip-png rf) (strip-png wf)) (= rf wf))
                (note "the transcripts differ: rust " (some-> rf keys vec) " wasm " (some-> wf keys vec)))
              (when-not (same? ref rep) (note "wasm replaying rust's transcript differs: " (first-diff ref rep)))))))
      (fs/delete-tree outd)
      {:probs @probs :jobs (count jobs)})))

(defn wasm-pass
  "The browser over `items` (the same inputs and flags the other arms had): byte-identical to the reference on every adapter, its recording the
  one Rust makes, its replay of Rust's. Prints the score, or the differences."
  [label items]
  (let [t1 (System/currentTimeMillis)
        base (str work "/wasm-" label)
        _ (fs/create-dirs base)
        prep (vec (pmap (fn [[i item]]
                          (let [ref (drive :rust [] item)
                                rd (when (and (zero? (:exit ref)) (not (:replay item)))
                                     (let [d (str base "/" i "-rust")] (drive :rust [(str "--record=" d)] item) d))]
                            [i item ref rd]))
                        (map-indexed vector items)))
        res (doall (for [batch (partition-all 60 prep)] (wasm-batch label base batch)))
        probs (mapcat :probs res)]
    (doseq [[f t] probs] (bad "[wasm" (when (seq label) (str " " label)) "] " f ": " t))
    (when (empty? probs)
      (ok "IDENTITY (wasm" (when (seq label) (str ", " label)) "): " (count items) " inputs through the browser, " (str/join ", " wasm-adapters)
          ": byte-identical to the reference bundle, exit and stderr; its recorded transcript is Rust's, and it replays Rust's ("
          (reduce + (map :jobs res)) " conversions, " (quot (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t1) 1000) " s)"))))

;; ----------------------------------------------------------------- the run

(println (str "  identity: " (count corpus*) " inputs x " (count arms) " arms + the transcript trip"
              (when full? " (--full)") (when corpus? " (--corpus: the public corpus, not the committed one)")))
(def t0 (System/currentTimeMillis))
(def results (doall (pmap (fn [[i item]] [item (one i item)]) (map-indexed vector corpus*))))
(doseq [[item {:keys [probs]}] results :when (seq probs)]
  (bad (:file item) (when (:pw item) (str " (password " (:pw item) ")")) ": " (str/join "; " probs)))
(def cov-main (coverage "main" results))

(when (zero? @fails)
  (let [outcomes (frequencies (map (comp :outcome second) results))
        docs (get outcomes :document 0)]
    (ok "IDENTITY: " (count results) " inputs (" docs " converted, " (- (count results) docs) " refused by name: "
        (str/join ", " (for [[k v] (sort-by (comp str key) (dissoc outcomes :document))] (str k " " v)))
        "), " (count arms) " arms each, byte-identical bundles (JSON compact and pretty, HTML default and full, evidence, intake) and exit and stderr; "
        "the record/replay trip across hosts is the same (" (quot (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0) 1000) " s)")
    (ok "COVERAGE (main): every host saw every input on every arm: " cov-main)))

;; the browser, over the same corpus (P9.3)
(when (and wasm (not corpus?) (zero? @fails))
  (wasm-pass "" (vec corpus*)))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- the assets pass (P3.13)

(def asset-corpus
  (vec (for [f (concat (globs "test/assets" "*.pdf")
                       (map #(str "test/corpus/synth/pdf/" % ".pdf")
                            ["figures-charts" "figures-logo-screenshot" "initial-image" "gfx-image-rules"
                             "mixed-table-image-shaded" "mixed-table-image" "columns-span-figure"]))
             :when (and (fs/exists? f) (or (not only) (str/includes? f only)))
             ;; P6.1a: a lossy codec is not the same pixel for pixel on two hosts (D190), so a document whose images the host decodes is
             ;; run from the transcript `bb asset-record` made (its pixels are the recording's), by every arm
             :let [tr (str "test/assets/transcripts/" (fs/strip-ext (fs/file-name f)))]]
         {:file f :pw nil :replay (when (fs/exists? (str tr "/transcript.edn")) tr)})))

(when (and (not corpus?) (zero? @fails))
  (reset! extra ["--assets=images"])
  (let [t1 (System/currentTimeMillis)
        res (doall (pmap (fn [[i item]] [item (one (+ 100000 i) item)]) (map-indexed vector asset-corpus)))]
    (doseq [[item {:keys [probs]}] res :when (seq probs)]
      (bad "[assets=images] " (:file item) ": " (str/join "; " probs)))
    (let [cov (coverage "assets=images" res)]
      (when (zero? @fails)
        (let [n (count (filter #(= :document (:outcome (second %))) res))]
          (ok "IDENTITY (assets=images): " (count res) " documents (" n " converted), " (count arms) " arms each: byte-identical JSON with its `assets`, HTML in the "
              "default, full, external and omit modes and every asset file (hex), the record/replay trip across hosts the same ("
              (quot (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t1) 1000) " s)")
          (ok "COVERAGE (assets=images): " cov)))))
  (when (and wasm (zero? @fails))
    (wasm-pass "assets" asset-corpus)))

;; ----------------------------------------------------------- the figures pass (P8.5, D351)
;; AND AT `figures`: the asset unit asks for `crop`s and `decode`s, which a driver with no Renderer answers `unsupported` (D199): on every arm the
;; same figures with the same reasons (`render`), the same vector regions found, and the same TRANSCRIPT written, entries for the requests and
;; all (each host replays the other's). The live pixels of the crops are `bb asset`'s (the committed pdfium transcripts).
(def figures-corpus
  (vec (for [f (concat (globs "test/assets/fig" "*.pdf")
                       (map #(str "test/assets/" % ".pdf") ["dct-rgb" "flate-rgb8" "place-twice" "place-skew" "place-clip-circle" "place-rot90" "smask" "dct-smask" "jpx"])
                       (map #(str "test/corpus/synth/pdf/" % ".pdf")
                            ["figures-charts" "figures-logo-screenshot" "columns-span-figure" "mixed-table-image" "table-simple-ruled" "bank-statement"]))
             :when (and (fs/exists? f) (or (not only) (str/includes? f only)))
             ;; as at `images` (P6.1a): a document whose images the host decodes is run from the transcript `bb asset-record` made
             :let [tr (str "test/assets/transcripts/" (fs/strip-ext (fs/file-name f)))]]
         {:file f :pw nil :replay (when (fs/exists? (str tr "/transcript.edn")) tr)})))

(when (and (not corpus?) (zero? @fails))
  (reset! extra ["--assets=figures"])
  (let [t2 (System/currentTimeMillis)
        res (doall (pmap (fn [[i item]] [item (one (+ 200000 i) item)]) (map-indexed vector figures-corpus)))]
    (doseq [[item {:keys [probs]}] res :when (seq probs)]
      (bad "[assets=figures] " (:file item) ": " (str/join "; " probs)))
    (let [cov (coverage "assets=figures" res)]
      (when (zero? @fails)
        (let [n (count (filter #(= :document (:outcome (second %))) res))]
          (ok "IDENTITY (assets=figures): " (count res) " documents (" n " converted), " (count arms) " arms each: byte-identical JSON, HTML in four modes and asset files, "
              "and the transcript of the asset unit's requests, the same on every host and replayed across them (" (quot (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t2) 1000) " s)")
          (ok "COVERAGE (assets=figures): " cov)))))
  ;; the browser at `figures` too (P9.5, D494): its session answers `render` and `crop` `unsupported` as the drivers do (D199)
  (when (and wasm (zero? @fails))
    (wasm-pass "figures" figures-corpus)))

(if (zero? @fails)
  (System/exit 0)
  (do (println "  FAIL" @fails "input(s) differ") (System/exit 1)))
